  "_toolbox": {
    "status": "tested",
    "testedOn": "UPS widgets: a production Polaris install (exported 2026-10-23); PDU widgets: an AP8870 on a production install 2026-11-11 (per-phase / per-bank / energy widgets added after that run, built from PowerNet-MIB and the PDU's web page)",
    "date": "2026-10-23",
    "note": "One APC profile governs every APC product, so every widget is scoped by modelPattern. UPS widgets (w1-w8, PowerNet-MIB ups*) carry 'UPS|Symmetra|Galaxy' — UPS models come from this profile's upsBasicIdentModel row. Rack PDU widgets (rPDU2*) carry '^(AP8|APDU)' — a 2G/3G rack PDU's model comes from its management card's sysDescr (MN:AP8870, Polaris rule 161). Per-phase and per-bank widgets name ONE table row with a row suffix (rPDU2PhaseStatusPower.2 = L2, rPDU2BankStatusCurrent.3 = bank 3), which needs Polaris from 2026-11-11; an older install does not resolve the suffixed symbol and the widget stays empty. kW / kVA / power factor use hundredths_to_units (also 2026-11-11). Run on an AP8870 (2-phase 208 V, 3 banks) 2026-11-11: power, L1 current, voltage, load / power-supply states read correctly; that model has 0 metered and 0 switched outlets, so Outlet Power is scoped to '^(AP89|APDU)' and Outlet State to '^(AP86|AP89|APDU)' (family letters from APC's numbering, not tested). A single-phase PDU has no L2 row and a non-banked one no bank rows — switch those widgets off there. Probe Temperature (rPDU2SensorTempHumidityStatusTempC) is not shipped: with no probe attached the PDU answers -1 (TempStatus notPresent), which a gauge cannot tell from a reading; add it by hand, switched on only for PDUs with a probe fitted."
  }
}
